<article class="env-definition" id="07H9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07H9">Definition <span data-tag="07H9">60.2.2</span>.</a> Let $(A, I, \gamma )$ be a divided power ring. Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. Let $J \subset B$ be an ideal with $IB \subset J$. The divided power algebra $(D, \bar J, \bar\gamma )$ constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/07H8" data-tag="07H8">60.2.1</a> is called the <em>divided power envelope of $J$ in $B$ relative to $(A, I, \gamma )$</em> and is denoted $D_ B(J)$ or $D_{B, \gamma }(J)$. </p>
</article>